# Regenerable forge artifacts — excluded from the registry commit.
# Recreate per-project with setup_poc.sh + `forge build`.
out/
cache/
broadcast/
.run.lock

# Per-POC regenerable traces / runner dumps (not source of record).
20*/20*.json
20*/forge_trace.json
20*/forge_trace.json.stderr
20*/attack_tx.json
20*/forge_trace.txt

# Per-POC lib/ contents are NOT committed, EXCEPT the forge-std symlink that each POC
# needs to resolve to _shared/forge-std. We force-add those symlinks; everything else
# under <poc>/lib/ (if any) is ignored.
lib/*
!lib/forge-std

# Single committed forge-std copy lives under _shared/forge-std (tracked in full).
# (the lib/ ignore above is per-poc; _shared/forge-std is not under a <poc>/lib.)

# Test-run output (regenerated)
_shared/results/

# macOS
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Editor / OS cruft
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db

# Keep the valuable products: anvil_state.json, output.txt, *.md, sources/,
# foundry.toml, test/, interface.sol, _shared/ tooling — all committed.

# ── Synthetic-exploit build artifacts (AUTO-MANAGED) ─────────────────────────
# Each is scripts/poc-configs/synthetic/<file> copied into <poc>/test/<file> by the
# crypto-training EVM Playground build (build-poc-runner-data.mjs) and recompiled on
# every build. Source-of-record lives in crypto-training; these must NOT be committed
# as duplicates of the canonical <Name>_exp.sol. New entries are appended automatically
# by the build. See docs/De-duplication.md.

